        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469">

                <pb facs="0437" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 093.11141/23.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador Page.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 303
                    of the 29th ultimo, covering a copy of a note from the Foreign Office making
                    formal acceptance on the part of the British Government of the gift of a replica
                    of Houdon’s statue of Washington offered by the State of Virginia.</p>
                <p>It has afforded the Department pleasure to communicate copies of your despatch
                    and of its enclosure to the Governor of Virginia with reference to the previous
                    correspondence.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
